[00:00.42]Execution is the ability to turn ideas into action.|执行力，就是把想法变成行动的能力。
[00:04.82]Many people have goals and plans, but they still get no results.|很多人有目标和计划，却依然没有结果。
[00:09.44]The problem is often not a lack of ability, but a lack of execution.|问题往往不在于能力不足，而在于执行力不够。
[00:14.88]Execution decides whether you can truly move forward and how far you can go.|执行力决定了你是否真的能往前走，以及能走多远。
[00:20.54]In learning, execution is especially important.|在学习上，执行力尤其重要。
[00:24.44]Many people know they should study every day.|很多人知道应该每天学习。
[00:26.48]They also know they should review, practice, and reflect.|也知道应该复习、练习和反思。
[00:31.22]But they often stay at the stage of knowing.|但他们常常停留在「知道」这一步。
[00:34.42]They plan to study today, then delay it tomorrow.|今天打算学，明天又往后拖。
[00:38.04]Their plans look good, but they rarely follow them.|计划看起来很漂亮，却很少真正执行。
[00:41.92]Over time, the gap becomes larger.|时间一长，差距就越来越大。
[00:45.00]Learning is not about how much you know, but how much you actually do.|学习不在于你知道多少，而在于你真正做了多少。
[00:50.08]Learning execution means doing simple things again and again.|练执行力，就是把简单的事一遍一遍地做。
[00:54.70]Finish your daily tasks on time.|按时完成每天的任务。
[00:57.46]Don't make excuses.|不要找借口。
[00:59.18]Don't give up easily.|不要轻易放弃。
[01:01.18]Even if you improve just a little every day, you will see big changes over time.|哪怕每天只进步一点点，时间久了也会有巨大的变化。
[01:07.18]People with strong execution are not always smarter, but they are more consistent.|执行力强的人未必更聪明，但他们更持久。
[01:13.14]They do not rely on short-term motivation.|他们不依赖一时的动力。
[01:15.68]They rely on daily action.|他们依靠每天的行动。
[01:18.84]When it comes to learning English, execution is even more important.|说到学英语，执行力就更重要了。
[01:23.36]Many people think English is difficult.|很多人觉得英语很难。
[01:26.10]In fact, the real challenge is not the content, but consistency.|其实真正的挑战不在内容，而在坚持。
[01:31.62]Everyone knows they should learn vocabulary, listen more, and speak more.|人人都知道该背单词、多听、多说。
[01:37.58]But only a few people actually do these things every day.|但真正每天去做的人寥寥无几。
[01:41.12]Some people learn many methods, but they rarely put them into practice, so they make little progress.|有些人学了很多方法，却很少付诸实践，所以进步很小。
[01:48.28]Learning English takes time, and execution keeps you on track.|学英语需要时间，而执行力让你不跑偏。
[01:53.66]Listen to English every day so your ears get used to the sound.|每天听英语，让耳朵熟悉这种声音。
[01:58.36]Learn a few new words each day so your vocabulary grows.|每天学几个新词，让词汇量增长。
[02:03.10]Say a few simple sentences daily so speaking becomes more natural.|每天说几个简单的句子，让口语变得自然。
[02:08.56]These actions may seem small, but if you keep doing them for a year, the results will be clear.|这些行动看起来很小，但坚持一年，结果会很明显。
[02:14.84]Many people fail not because their methods are wrong, but because they do not keep going.|很多人失败不是因为方法错，而是因为没有坚持。
[02:20.46]They study for a short time and then stop.|他们学一阵子就停下了。
[02:23.26]When they don't see quick results, they begin to doubt themselves.|看不到快速的效果，就开始怀疑自己。
[02:27.20]But language learning is a slow process.|但语言学习本来就是个缓慢的过程。
[02:30.36]It needs time and patience.|它需要时间和耐心。
[02:32.96]Execution means continuing even when you cannot see results yet.|执行力意味着：在还看不到结果的时候依然继续。
[02:37.70]To improve execution, start with small steps.|想提升执行力，从小步开始。
[02:42.38]Set simple goals such as studying for 20 minutes a day or listening to one short audio clip.|定一些简单的目标，比如每天学 20 分钟，或者听一段短音频。
[02:49.24]Don't expect too much at the beginning or you may give up.|一开始别期望太高，否则容易放弃。
[02:53.44]After you finish your task, give yourself a small reward.|完成任务后，给自己一点小奖励。
[02:57.92]This makes learning easier and more enjoyable.|这会让学习更轻松、更有趣。
[03:01.34]At the same time, reduce distractions, stay away from your phone while studying, focus on one thing at a time.|同时减少干扰：学习时远离手机，一次只专注一件事。
[03:09.58]The time does not need to be long, but it should be focused.|时间不必很长，但必须专注。
[03:14.42]20 minutes of deep focus is often more effective than one hour of low-quality work.|20 分钟深度专注，往往比一小时低效的忙碌更有效。
[03:21.24]Execution is not something you are born with.|执行力不是天生的。
[03:24.86]It can be built over time.|它可以慢慢培养。
[03:27.00]As long as you take action every day, you will become more disciplined.|只要你每天行动，就会越来越自律。
[03:32.46]Slowly, persistence itself becomes a habit.|慢慢地，坚持本身就成了一种习惯。
[03:35.90]Learning English is the same.|学英语也是一样。
[03:37.30]Don't stay at the level of thinking|不要停留在「想一想」，
[03:39.86]Start taking action today|从今天就开始行动。
[03:42.46]Even a small step is better than doing nothing|哪怕一小步，也胜过什么都不做。
[03:45.84]As long as you keep going, you will see results|只要坚持下去，你一定会看到结果。
[03:49.40]Execution is the key that turns wanting to learn English into actually mastering it|执行力，就是把「想学英语」变成「真正掌握」的那把钥匙。
